WEBVTT

00:00:20.803 --> 00:00:22.310
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:22.316 --> 00:00:23.885
Let's say good night to your brother.

00:00:24.088 --> 00:00:25.148
Night, Sam.

00:00:25.272 --> 00:00:26.652
Hey, Dean.

00:00:26.677 --> 00:00:28.206
Daddy! Hey, buddy.

00:00:29.127 --> 00:00:30.734
Sweet dreams, Sam.

00:00:34.892 --> 00:00:37.370
Dad's missing. I need
you to help me find him.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:39.317
The trail for dad, it's getting colder.

00:00:39.441 --> 00:00:42.031
Every day. You don't think I want
to find dad as much as you do?

00:00:42.055 --> 00:00:43.433
I know you do. Find dad.

00:00:43.457 --> 00:00:45.750
Mom's gone. She isn't coming back.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.151
Don't talk about her like that.

00:01:13.344 --> 00:01:14.599
Mommy?

00:01:16.259 --> 00:01:18.188
Hey, sweetie.

00:01:18.464 --> 00:01:22.413
Why aren't you in bed?
There's something in my closet.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:39.071
See?

00:01:39.106 --> 00:01:40.385
There's nothing there.

00:01:41.763 --> 00:01:44.702
You're sure? I'm sure.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:52.990
Now, come on.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.101
Into bed.

00:02:01.544 --> 00:02:03.167
I don't like this house.

00:02:03.782 --> 00:02:05.381
You're just not used to it yet.

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:12.045
But you and your brother and me,
we are going to be very happy here.

00:02:12.596 --> 00:02:13.604
I promise.

00:02:16.209 --> 00:02:17.864
I love you.

00:02:25.664 --> 00:02:26.417
The chair.

00:02:27.299 --> 00:02:28.712
Okay.

00:02:29.351 --> 00:02:30.329
Right.

00:02:34.204 --> 00:02:35.258
The chair.

00:02:37.879 --> 00:02:39.572
Just to be safe.

00:03:11.812 --> 00:03:15.348
Please, god, don't let it be rats.

00:03:35.057 --> 00:03:36.294
Terrific.

00:05:33.885 --> 00:05:34.578
All right.

00:05:34.603 --> 00:05:36.400
I've been cruising some websites.

00:05:36.505 --> 00:05:38.899
Think I found a few
candidates for our next gig.

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:42.963
A fishing trawler found
off the coast of Cali.

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:44.486
Its crew vanished.

00:05:44.717 --> 00:05:48.200
And we got some cattle
mutilations in west Texas.

00:05:48.682 --> 00:05:49.299
Hey!

00:05:51.131 --> 00:05:53.193
Am I boring you with
this hunting-Evil stuff?

00:05:53.733 --> 00:05:55.815
No, I'm listening. Keep going.

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:00.596
And here a Sacramento man
shot himself in the head...

00:06:01.039 --> 00:06:02.273
Three times.

00:06:04.711 --> 00:06:06.754
Any of these things
blowing up your skirt, pal?

00:06:10.783 --> 00:06:12.817
Wait, I've seen this. Seen what?

00:06:19.678 --> 00:06:20.791
What are you doing?

00:06:29.132 --> 00:06:30.872
Dean, I know where we have to go next.

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:31.584
Where?

00:06:32.213 --> 00:06:33.151
Back home.

00:06:33.965 --> 00:06:34.989
Back to Kansas.

00:06:36.383 --> 00:06:38.258
Okay, random. Where'd that come from?

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:40.152
All right, um...

00:06:40.192 --> 00:06:42.521
This photo was taken in
front of our old house, right?

00:06:42.606 --> 00:06:43.821
The house where mom died?

00:06:45.266 --> 00:06:45.922
Yeah.

00:06:45.999 --> 00:06:49.161
It didn't burn down right? I mean not
completely, they rebuilt it, right?

00:06:49.238 --> 00:06:51.590
I guess so, yeah. What the
hell are you talking about?

00:06:51.621 --> 00:06:53.831
Okay, look, this is gonna sound crazy,

00:06:53.861 --> 00:06:55.944
But the people who
live in our old house,

00:06:57.212 --> 00:06:58.851
I think they might be in danger.

00:06:59.196 --> 00:07:01.566
Why would you think that? Uh...

00:07:01.624 --> 00:07:03.646
Just, um... look, just...

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:05.030
You got to trust me on this, okay?

00:07:06.667 --> 00:07:08.736
Hey, whoa, whoa, whoa. Trust you? Yeah.

00:07:09.254 --> 00:07:11.158
You got to give me a
little bit more than that.

00:07:11.204 --> 00:07:12.936
I can't really explain, it is all.

00:07:13.141 --> 00:07:15.665
Well, tough. I'm not going
anywhere until you do.

00:07:20.327 --> 00:07:22.023
I have these nightmares.

00:07:22.324 --> 00:07:23.728
I've noticed.

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:28.514
And sometimes they come true.

00:07:31.566 --> 00:07:32.574
Come again?

00:07:33.437 --> 00:07:34.116
Look, Dean...

00:07:35.309 --> 00:07:36.773
I dreamt about Jessica's death

00:07:37.572 --> 00:07:39.484
For days before it happened.

00:07:42.083 --> 00:07:44.827
Sane people have weird dreams, man.
I'm sure it's just a coincidence.

00:07:45.376 --> 00:07:48.510
No, I dreamt about the blood dripping,
her on the ceiling, the fire, everything,

00:07:48.522 --> 00:07:50.389
And I didn't do anything
'cause I didn't believe it.

00:07:50.447 --> 00:07:52.067
Now I'm dreaming about that tree,

00:07:52.236 --> 00:07:55.087
About our house, and some woman
inside screaming for help. I mean,

00:07:55.276 --> 00:07:57.716
That's where it all started, man.
This has to mean something, right?

00:07:59.991 --> 00:08:00.824
I don't know.

00:08:01.844 --> 00:08:04.025
What do you mean you
don't know, Dean? This...

00:08:04.143 --> 00:08:05.832
This woman might be in danger.

00:08:05.891 --> 00:08:10.031
This might be the thing that killed mom and
Jessica. All right, just slow down,would you?

00:08:14.066 --> 00:08:16.670
I mean, first you're telling
me that you've got this Shining

00:08:17.879 --> 00:08:19.756
and then you tell me that
I've got to go back home,

00:08:20.999 --> 00:08:21.922
Especially when...

00:08:23.905 --> 00:08:25.009
When what?

00:08:26.427 --> 00:08:28.714
When I swore to myself that
I would never go back there.

00:08:40.115 --> 00:08:42.062
Dean, we have to check this out.

00:08:43.208 --> 00:08:44.608
Just to make sure.

00:08:51.936 --> 00:08:53.027
I know we do.

00:09:11.466 --> 00:09:13.066
You gonna be all right, man?

00:09:14.967 --> 00:09:16.793
Let me get back to you on that.

00:09:24.865 --> 00:09:25.358
Yes?

00:09:25.628 --> 00:09:26.988
Sorry to bother you, ma'am,

00:09:27.099 --> 00:09:29.492
But we're with the
federal... I'm Sam Winchester

00:09:29.726 --> 00:09:31.486
And this is my brother, Dean.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:33.884
Um...we used to live here.

00:09:34.799 --> 00:09:37.169
You know, we were just driving by, and

00:09:37.222 --> 00:09:39.603
We were wondering if we
could come see the old place.

00:09:39.664 --> 00:09:40.825
Winchester...

00:09:42.362 --> 00:09:43.817
That is so funny.

00:09:44.013 --> 00:09:47.333
You know, I, I think I found some
of your photos the other night.

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:48.025
You did?

00:09:52.291 --> 00:09:54.441
Okay. Come on in.

00:10:06.381 --> 00:10:08.446
Juice, juice, juice!

00:10:08.481 --> 00:10:10.399
Juice, juice,  juice!

00:10:10.422 --> 00:10:14.293
That's Richie. He's
kind of a juice junkie.

00:10:14.532 --> 00:10:17.499
But, hey, at least he won't get scurvy.

00:10:18.755 --> 00:10:19.857
Sari,

00:10:20.268 --> 00:10:22.368
This is Sam and Dean.

00:10:22.416 --> 00:10:24.351
They used to live here. Hi.

00:10:24.879 --> 00:10:25.817
Hey, Sari.

00:10:26.768 --> 00:10:28.070
So, you just moved in?

00:10:28.128 --> 00:10:29.853
Uh, yeah, from Wichita.

00:10:29.955 --> 00:10:31.375
You got family here?

00:10:32.466 --> 00:10:34.436
No, I just, uh...

00:10:35.598 --> 00:10:38.759
Um, needed a fresh start. That's all.

00:10:39.888 --> 00:10:42.089
So new town,

00:10:42.199 --> 00:10:43.317
New job

00:10:43.501 --> 00:10:45.333
I mean, as soon as I find one,

00:10:45.737 --> 00:10:47.001
New house.

00:10:49.056 --> 00:10:50.816
So, how you liking it so far?

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:55.783
Well, uh, all due respect
to your childhood home,

00:10:55.875 --> 00:10:59.320
I mean, I'm sure you have
lots of happy memories here,

00:10:59.778 --> 00:11:02.051
But this place has its issues.

00:11:02.326 --> 00:11:03.536
What do you mean?

00:11:04.909 --> 00:11:06.706
Well, it's just getting old

00:11:07.109 --> 00:11:09.235
Like, the wiring, you know? We've got

00:11:09.363 --> 00:11:11.471
Flickering lights almost hourly.

00:11:11.581 --> 00:11:12.827
Oh, that's too bad.

00:11:13.304 --> 00:11:14.330
What else?

00:11:14.678 --> 00:11:18.986
Um...sink's backed up.
There's rats in the basement.

00:11:21.096 --> 00:11:22.526
I'm sorry.

00:11:22.691 --> 00:11:24.798
I don't mean to complain. No.

00:11:24.872 --> 00:11:28.262
Have you seen the rats or
have you just heard scratching?

00:11:29.344 --> 00:11:32.386
Just the scratching, actually. Mom?

00:11:36.784 --> 00:11:39.790
Ask them if it was here
when they lived here.

00:11:41.183 --> 00:11:42.228
What, Sari?

00:11:43.016 --> 00:11:44.739
The thing in my closet.

00:11:44.769 --> 00:11:49.056
Oh, no, baby, there was
nothing in their closets.

00:11:49.209 --> 00:11:50.011
Right?

00:11:50.836 --> 00:11:53.083
Right, no.No, of course not.

00:11:54.345 --> 00:11:56.958
She had a nightmare the other night.

00:11:57.073 --> 00:11:58.586
I wasn't dreaming.

00:11:58.770 --> 00:12:02.186
It came into my bedroom,
and it was on fire.

00:12:03.179 --> 00:12:06.114
You heard that ? A figure on fire.

00:12:06.437 --> 00:12:08.785
And that woman Jenny, that was
the woman in your dreams? Yeah.

00:12:08.857 --> 00:12:11.607
And you hear what she was talking
about ? Scratching, flickering lights ?

00:12:11.683 --> 00:12:13.907
Both signs of a malevolent
spirit. Yeah well.

00:12:14.022 --> 00:12:16.161
I'm just freaked out your
weirdo visions are coming true.

00:12:16.177 --> 00:12:17.347
Forget about that for a minute.

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:20.213
The thing in the house, do you think it's the
thing that killed mom and Jessica? I don't know!

00:12:20.439 --> 00:12:22.474
Has it come back or has it
been there the whole time?

00:12:22.479 --> 00:12:24.824
Maybe it's something else
entirely. Sam, we don't know yet.

00:12:24.833 --> 00:12:26.607
Those people are in danger, Dean.

00:12:27.023 --> 00:12:28.992
We have to get them out
of that house. And we will.

00:12:29.022 --> 00:12:30.832
No, I mean now. And how
you're gonna do that ?

00:12:30.849 --> 00:12:33.477
You got a story she's gonna believe?
Then what are we supposed to do?!

00:12:34.013 --> 00:12:35.741
We just got to chill out, that's all.

00:12:36.596 --> 00:12:38.953
If this was any other kind
of job, what would we do?

00:12:44.052 --> 00:12:45.949
We'd try to figure out
what we were dealing with.

00:12:46.503 --> 00:12:49.042
We'd dig into the history
of the house. Exactly.

00:12:49.065 --> 00:12:50.601
Except this time we
already know what happened.

00:12:50.634 --> 00:12:54.230
Yeah, but how much do we know?
How much do you actually remember?

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:58.118
About that night, you mean? Yeah.

00:13:00.063 --> 00:13:01.032
Not much.

00:13:02.484 --> 00:13:03.849
I remember the fire...

00:13:04.847 --> 00:13:05.742
The heat.

00:13:09.662 --> 00:13:11.158
Then I carried you out the front door.

00:13:13.902 --> 00:13:14.739
You did?

00:13:16.559 --> 00:13:17.982
Yeah, well, you never knew that?

00:13:20.309 --> 00:13:21.150
No.

00:13:23.090 --> 00:13:24.088
And, uh...

00:13:24.161 --> 00:13:26.641
Well, you know dad's story
as well as I do. Mom was...

00:13:28.182 --> 00:13:29.253
Was on the ceiling.

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:32.555
Whatever put her there was long
gone by the time dad found her.

00:13:33.583 --> 00:13:36.277
And he never had a
theory about what did it?

00:13:36.782 --> 00:13:38.353
If he did, he kept it to himself.

00:13:39.264 --> 00:13:41.538
God knows we asked him enough times.

00:13:44.488 --> 00:13:45.324
Okay.

00:13:46.235 --> 00:13:48.744
So, if we're gonna figure
out what's going on now,

00:13:50.109 --> 00:13:51.914
We have to figure out
what happened back then,

00:13:53.191 --> 00:13:54.790
And see if it's the same thing.

00:13:54.952 --> 00:13:55.421
Yeah.

00:13:56.815 --> 00:13:59.904
Talk to dad's friends, neighbors,
people who were there at the time.

00:14:01.824 --> 00:14:04.125
Does this feel like
just another job to you?

00:14:10.824 --> 00:14:12.599
I'll be right back. I
got to go to the bathroom.

00:14:31.190 --> 00:14:32.922
<i>This is John Winchester.</i>

00:14:32.994 --> 00:14:39.289
<i>If this is an emergency, call
my son Dean, 866 907 32 35.</i>

00:14:39.333 --> 00:14:39.847
Dad...

00:14:43.062 --> 00:14:45.515
I know I've left you messages before.

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:48.442
I don't even know if you get 'em.

00:14:51.441 --> 00:14:51.999
But

00:14:52.469 --> 00:14:53.584
I'm with Sam

00:14:54.626 --> 00:14:56.167
And we're in Lawrence,

00:14:57.179 --> 00:14:59.607
And there's something in our old house.

00:15:00.936 --> 00:15:03.688
I don't know if it's the
thing that killed mom or not,

00:15:05.151 --> 00:15:05.576
But...

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:09.982
I don't know what to do.

00:15:11.901 --> 00:15:12.679
So,

00:15:13.031 --> 00:15:15.293
Whatever you're doing,
if you could get here...

00:15:17.257 --> 00:15:18.123
Please.

00:15:20.751 --> 00:15:22.204
I need your help, dad.

00:15:27.282 --> 00:15:30.862
No, sir, nothing weird
down there. I promise.

00:15:31.361 --> 00:15:34.311
Sink just backed upon
its own. I'll take a look.

00:15:34.502 --> 00:15:35.426
Thanks.

00:15:36.556 --> 00:15:38.699
Oh, okay, I'll get out of your way.

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:24.743
So you and John Winchester, you
used to own this garage together?

00:17:24.816 --> 00:17:27.502
Yeah, we used to. A long time ago.

00:17:27.615 --> 00:17:28.495
Matter of fact,

00:17:28.715 --> 00:17:31.665
Must be 20 years since John disappeared.

00:17:31.809 --> 00:17:33.593
So, why are the cops
interested all of a sudden?

00:17:33.668 --> 00:17:37.660
Oh, we're reopening some of our unsolved cases,
and the Winchester disappearance is one of them.

00:17:37.754 --> 00:17:40.358
Uh-Huh. Well, what do you
want to know about John?

00:17:40.452 --> 00:17:42.692
Whatever you remember, you know.
Whatever sticks out in your mind.

00:17:46.228 --> 00:17:48.888
He was a stubborn
bastard. I remember that.

00:17:49.862 --> 00:17:51.059
And, uh...

00:17:51.117 --> 00:17:54.015
Oh, whatever the game, he
hated to lose, you know?

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:55.786
It was that whole marine thing.

00:17:56.830 --> 00:17:57.792
But, uh...

00:17:58.093 --> 00:17:59.536
Well, he sure loved Mary,

00:18:00.545 --> 00:18:02.034
And he doted on those kids.

00:18:02.515 --> 00:18:03.993
But that was before the fire.

00:18:05.081 --> 00:18:05.727
That's right.

00:18:06.043 --> 00:18:07.427
He ever talk about that night?

00:18:09.011 --> 00:18:09.606
No,

00:18:09.981 --> 00:18:11.025
Not at first.

00:18:11.717 --> 00:18:13.571
I think he was in shock. Right,

00:18:14.134 --> 00:18:15.529
But eventually,

00:18:16.597 --> 00:18:17.977
What did he say about it?

00:18:18.667 --> 00:18:21.504
Oh, he wasn't thinking
straight. He said, uh...

00:18:22.128 --> 00:18:25.613
He said something caused
that fire and killed Mary.

00:18:25.648 --> 00:18:26.678
He ever say what did it?

00:18:27.617 --> 00:18:30.136
Nothing did it. It was an accident.

00:18:30.537 --> 00:18:34.208
An electrical short in the
ceiling or walls or something.

00:18:36.156 --> 00:18:39.959
I begged him to get some
help, but... But what?

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:42.385
Oh, it just got worse and worse.

00:18:42.596 --> 00:18:43.135
How?

00:18:43.863 --> 00:18:47.382
Oh, he started reading
these strange old books.

00:18:47.417 --> 00:18:50.132
He started going to see
this palm reader in town.

00:18:50.305 --> 00:18:52.427
Palm reader? You have a name?

00:18:53.390 --> 00:18:54.479
No.

00:18:58.598 --> 00:19:02.030
All right, so, there are a few
psychics and palm readers in town.

00:19:02.065 --> 00:19:04.510
There's someone named
El Divino. There's...

00:19:04.675 --> 00:19:07.443
There's the mysterious Mr. Fortinsky.

00:19:07.559 --> 00:19:10.198
Uh, Missouri Moseley,
some dude -- Wait, wait...

00:19:10.281 --> 00:19:11.407
Missouri Moseley?

00:19:11.735 --> 00:19:12.193
What?

00:19:12.509 --> 00:19:13.424
That's a psychic?

00:19:14.034 --> 00:19:16.732
Uh...yeah.Yeah, I guess so.

00:19:20.359 --> 00:19:21.263
In dad's journal...

00:19:24.653 --> 00:19:25.927
Look at this.

00:19:27.555 --> 00:19:29.957
First page, first sentence. Read that.

00:19:30.902 --> 00:19:32.228
"I went to Missouri...

00:19:33.483 --> 00:19:35.060
And I learned the truth."

00:19:35.887 --> 00:19:37.699
I always thought he meant the state.

00:19:43.511 --> 00:19:44.989
All right, then.

00:19:45.388 --> 00:19:47.347
Don't you worry about a thing.

00:19:48.156 --> 00:19:49.904
Your wife is crazy about you.

00:19:53.321 --> 00:19:55.959
Whew! Poor bastard.

00:19:56.463 --> 00:19:58.774
His woman cold-Bangin'the gardener.

00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:01.809
Why didn't you tell him?

00:20:02.203 --> 00:20:04.369
People don't come here for the truth.

00:20:04.404 --> 00:20:06.232
They come for good news.

00:20:07.739 --> 00:20:08.537
Well?

00:20:08.701 --> 00:20:11.960
Sam and Dean, come on
already. I ain't got all day.

00:20:20.075 --> 00:20:21.753
Well, let me look at you.

00:20:23.477 --> 00:20:26.493
Oh, you boys grew up handsome.

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:29.973
And you were one
goofy-Looking kid, too.

00:20:31.732 --> 00:20:32.765
Sam.

00:20:35.685 --> 00:20:37.163
Oh, honey.

00:20:39.052 --> 00:20:42.219
I'm sorry about your girlfriend.

00:20:42.829 --> 00:20:44.465
And your father

00:20:46.157 --> 00:20:47.681
he's missing?

00:20:50.614 --> 00:20:52.248
How'd you know all that?

00:20:52.283 --> 00:20:52.890
Well,

00:20:53.957 --> 00:20:56.840
You were just thinking it, just now.

00:20:57.361 --> 00:20:59.279
Well, where is he? Is he okay?

00:20:59.907 --> 00:21:01.318
I don't know.

00:21:01.983 --> 00:21:02.992
Don't know?

00:21:04.059 --> 00:21:05.775
You're supposed to be a psychic, right?

00:21:06.441 --> 00:21:10.542
Boy, you see me sawing
some bony tramp in half?

00:21:10.577 --> 00:21:11.974
You think I'm a magician?

00:21:12.212 --> 00:21:15.325
I may be able to read thoughts
and sense energies in a room,

00:21:15.360 --> 00:21:17.548
But I can't just pull
facts out of thin air.

00:21:17.583 --> 00:21:18.021
Sit!

00:21:18.274 --> 00:21:18.904
Please.

00:21:28.994 --> 00:21:32.630
Boy, you put your foot on my coffee
table, I'm gonna whack you with a spoon.

00:21:32.665 --> 00:21:33.568
I didn't do anything.

00:21:33.653 --> 00:21:35.146
Well, you were thinking about it.

00:21:41.749 --> 00:21:43.384
Okay, so...

00:21:44.370 --> 00:21:45.140
Our dad.

00:21:46.004 --> 00:21:47.461
When did you first meet him?

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:49.549
He came for a reading

00:21:50.245 --> 00:21:52.996
A few days after the fire.

00:21:53.884 --> 00:21:57.242
I just told him what was
really out there in the dark.

00:21:57.387 --> 00:21:59.108
I guess you could say

00:22:00.374 --> 00:22:02.467
I drew back the curtains for him.

00:22:02.493 --> 00:22:03.573
What about the fire?

00:22:04.991 --> 00:22:07.633
Do you know about what killed our mom?

00:22:07.870 --> 00:22:08.734
A little.

00:22:09.674 --> 00:22:11.819
Your daddy took me to your house.

00:22:11.993 --> 00:22:13.771
He was hoping I could

00:22:13.916 --> 00:22:14.977
Sense the

00:22:15.446 --> 00:22:16.451
Echoes,

00:22:16.489 --> 00:22:18.507
The fingerprints of this thing.

00:22:18.865 --> 00:22:19.812
And could you?

00:22:20.393 --> 00:22:21.163
I don't...

00:22:22.954 --> 00:22:23.893
What was it?

00:22:24.578 --> 00:22:25.555
I don't know.

00:22:28.410 --> 00:22:30.251
But it was evil.

00:22:30.463 --> 00:22:34.858
Look, I feel just awful
about the poor man's hand,

00:22:35.851 --> 00:22:38.521
But how can I be held liable?

00:22:40.884 --> 00:22:41.467
Yeah, but

00:22:41.626 --> 00:22:43.730
I can't afford a lawyer.

00:22:46.181 --> 00:22:48.892
Okay, listen, y-You just
got to let me call you back.

00:22:50.067 --> 00:22:53.108
Richie, mommy's gonna be right back,

00:22:53.333 --> 00:22:54.075
Okay?

00:22:54.169 --> 00:22:55.014
Okay.

00:22:55.437 --> 00:22:56.064
Okay.

00:23:00.177 --> 00:23:01.135
So,

00:23:02.683 --> 00:23:05.383
You think something's
back in that house?

00:23:06.348 --> 00:23:07.877
Definitely.

00:23:11.013 --> 00:23:12.813
I don't understand.

00:23:13.386 --> 00:23:14.540
What?

00:23:17.199 --> 00:23:19.011
I haven't been back inside,

00:23:19.046 --> 00:23:23.443
But I've been keeping an eye on
the place, and it's been quiet.

00:23:23.687 --> 00:23:25.786
No sudden deaths, no

00:23:25.947 --> 00:23:27.665
Freak accidents.

00:23:27.700 --> 00:23:29.288
Why is it acting up now?

00:23:29.779 --> 00:23:30.633
I don't know.

00:23:31.370 --> 00:23:34.726
But dad going missing
and Jessica dying and

00:23:35.123 --> 00:23:36.677
Now this house,

00:23:37.188 --> 00:23:40.597
All happening at once. It just
feels like something's starting.

00:23:41.267 --> 00:23:43.392
That's a comforting thought.

00:24:14.438 --> 00:24:15.763
Juicy!

00:24:30.150 --> 00:24:34.031
Oh, baby, either we have
rats or mommy is going crazy.

00:24:34.745 --> 00:24:35.495
Richie?

00:24:38.229 --> 00:24:39.366
Richie?!

00:24:49.659 --> 00:24:51.997
Baby, where are you?!

00:25:00.328 --> 00:25:01.008
Wha...

00:25:09.117 --> 00:25:11.299
Mum! Oh, my god!

00:25:17.488 --> 00:25:18.661
Oh, baby!

00:25:21.724 --> 00:25:23.461
Sam, Dean,

00:25:23.836 --> 00:25:25.009
What are you doing here?

00:25:25.185 --> 00:25:26.276
Hey, Jenny.

00:25:26.546 --> 00:25:28.909
Um, this is our friend Missouri.

00:25:29.731 --> 00:25:33.068
If it's not too much trouble, we were
hoping to show her the house, you know,

00:25:33.231 --> 00:25:35.139
For old time's sake.

00:25:35.174 --> 00:25:37.428
No, you know, this isn't a good time.

00:25:37.463 --> 00:25:39.424
I'm kind of busy. Listen,
Jenny,it's important.

00:25:39.569 --> 00:25:40.058
Ow!

00:25:40.419 --> 00:25:43.738
Give the poor girl a break.
Can't you see she's upset?

00:25:43.773 --> 00:25:45.204
Forgive this boy. He means well.

00:25:45.239 --> 00:25:47.275
He's just not the
sharpest tool in the shed.

00:25:47.310 --> 00:25:48.691
But hear me out.

00:25:49.295 --> 00:25:50.401
About what?

00:25:50.459 --> 00:25:51.725
About this house.

00:25:52.520 --> 00:25:53.902
What are you talking about?

00:25:54.397 --> 00:25:57.125
I think you know what I'm talking about.

00:25:57.160 --> 00:26:02.091
You think there's something in this house,
something that wants to hurt your family.

00:26:02.126 --> 00:26:03.580
Am I mistaken?

00:26:04.514 --> 00:26:06.251
Who are you?

00:26:06.286 --> 00:26:09.554
We're people who can help,
who can stop this thing,

00:26:09.589 --> 00:26:12.042
But you're gonna have to
trust us, just a little.

00:26:14.764 --> 00:26:19.968
If there's a dark energy around here,
this room should be the center of it.

00:26:21.317 --> 00:26:22.128
Why?

00:26:22.658 --> 00:26:25.335
This used to be your nursery, Sam.

00:26:25.370 --> 00:26:27.646
This is where it all happened.

00:26:42.935 --> 00:26:44.612
That an emf?

00:26:45.006 --> 00:26:45.592
Yeah.

00:26:46.552 --> 00:26:47.399
Amateur.

00:26:57.764 --> 00:27:00.602
I don't know if you boys should
be disappointed or relieved,

00:27:00.637 --> 00:27:02.818
But this ain't the
thing that took your mom.

00:27:04.478 --> 00:27:05.906
Are you sure?

00:27:06.887 --> 00:27:08.113
How do you know?

00:27:08.119 --> 00:27:11.921
It isn't the same energy I
felt the last time I was here.

00:27:11.956 --> 00:27:13.368
It's something different.

00:27:14.353 --> 00:27:15.375
What is it?

00:27:17.004 --> 00:27:18.495
Not it...

00:27:19.253 --> 00:27:20.797
Them.

00:27:21.411 --> 00:27:24.478
There's more than one
spirit in this place.

00:27:25.634 --> 00:27:27.246
What are they doing here?

00:27:27.281 --> 00:27:30.140
They're here because of
what happened to your family.

00:27:30.734 --> 00:27:32.636
You see, all those years ago,

00:27:32.728 --> 00:27:35.268
Real evil came to you.

00:27:36.648 --> 00:27:41.242
It walked this house. That
kind of evil leaves wounds,

00:27:41.277 --> 00:27:44.050
And sometimes wounds get infected.

00:27:44.366 --> 00:27:46.098
I don't understand.

00:27:46.133 --> 00:27:49.408
This place is a magnet
for paranormal energy.

00:27:52.222 --> 00:27:54.632
It's attracted a poltergeist,

00:27:55.087 --> 00:27:56.760
A nasty one,

00:27:57.527 --> 00:28:01.288
And it won't rest until
Jenny and her babies are dead.

00:28:01.323 --> 00:28:03.552
You said there was more than one spirit.

00:28:03.641 --> 00:28:05.144
There is.

00:28:08.004 --> 00:28:11.301
I just can't quite
make out the second one.

00:28:15.361 --> 00:28:17.205
Well, one thing's for damn sure,

00:28:17.793 --> 00:28:19.630
Nobody's dying in this house,

00:28:19.665 --> 00:28:20.804
Ever again.

00:28:21.484 --> 00:28:23.835
So, whatever is here, how do we stop it?

00:28:27.249 --> 00:28:29.370
So, what is all this stuff anyway?

00:28:29.811 --> 00:28:33.250
Angelica root, van van
oil, crossroad dirt,

00:28:33.305 --> 00:28:35.241
A few other odds and ends.

00:28:35.276 --> 00:28:36.505
What are we supposed to do with it?

00:28:36.540 --> 00:28:39.712
We're gonna put them inside the walls

00:28:39.928 --> 00:28:43.160
In the north, south, east, west corners

00:28:43.195 --> 00:28:45.127
On each floor of the house.

00:28:45.162 --> 00:28:48.270
Punching holes in the drywall.
Jenny's gonna love that.

00:28:49.230 --> 00:28:50.647
She'll live.

00:28:51.715 --> 00:28:53.958
And this will destroy the spirits?

00:28:53.993 --> 00:28:55.270
It should.

00:28:55.840 --> 00:28:58.461
It should purify the house completely.

00:28:59.604 --> 00:29:01.270
We'll each take a floor,

00:29:01.633 --> 00:29:03.143
But we work fast.

00:29:03.178 --> 00:29:06.039
Once the spirits
realize what we're up to,

00:29:06.067 --> 00:29:08.198
Things are gonna get bad.

00:29:09.969 --> 00:29:10.821
Okay.

00:29:12.151 --> 00:29:13.534
Careful.

00:29:15.037 --> 00:29:18.847
Look, I -You know, I'm not sure I'm
comfortable leaving you guys here alone.

00:29:18.882 --> 00:29:21.181
Just take your kids to
the movie or something, and

00:29:21.219 --> 00:29:23.373
It'll be over by the time you get back.

00:29:24.245 --> 00:29:24.937
Okay.

00:30:21.621 --> 00:30:23.372
Aah! Uhh!

00:31:01.430 --> 00:31:02.205
Sam!

00:31:04.516 --> 00:31:05.255
Sam!

00:31:28.277 --> 00:31:29.469
Come on.

00:31:51.245 --> 00:31:53.130
Are you sure this is over?

00:31:56.299 --> 00:31:57.609
I'm sure.

00:31:58.037 --> 00:31:58.646
Why?

00:31:59.796 --> 00:32:01.483
Why do you ask?

00:32:02.338 --> 00:32:03.929
No, never mind.

00:32:05.634 --> 00:32:07.481
It's nothing, I guess.

00:32:09.517 --> 00:32:10.840
Hello?

00:32:11.417 --> 00:32:12.896
We're home.

00:32:15.933 --> 00:32:17.541
What happened?

00:32:17.645 --> 00:32:20.316
Hi. Sorry. Um, we'll...

00:32:20.351 --> 00:32:22.381
We'll pay for all of this.

00:32:23.143 --> 00:32:24.575
Don't you worry.

00:32:24.633 --> 00:32:26.698
Dean's gonna clean up this mess.

00:32:29.724 --> 00:32:31.707
Well, what are you waiting for, boy?

00:32:31.742 --> 00:32:32.510
Get the mop.

00:32:33.414 --> 00:32:34.974
And don't cuss at me.

00:32:56.504 --> 00:32:57.267
Okay.

00:33:51.226 --> 00:33:53.331
So, tell me again. What
are we still doing here?

00:33:53.366 --> 00:33:54.827
I don't know, I-I just...

00:33:55.472 --> 00:33:57.056
I still have a bad feeling.

00:33:57.642 --> 00:33:58.651
Why?

00:33:59.167 --> 00:34:02.812
Missouri did her whole zelda rubenstein thing.
The house should be clean. This should be over.

00:34:03.037 --> 00:34:05.946
Yeah, probably, but I just
want to make sure. That's all.

00:34:07.410 --> 00:34:10.466
The problem is I could be
sleeping in a bed right now.

00:34:14.837 --> 00:34:15.775
Dean!

00:34:16.256 --> 00:34:16.956
Dean!

00:34:18.915 --> 00:34:20.759
You grab the kids, I'll get Jenny.

00:34:39.418 --> 00:34:41.119
Come on! Jenny!

00:34:41.157 --> 00:34:43.775
I can't open the door! Stand back!

00:34:46.841 --> 00:34:48.342
Come on! No, my kids!

00:34:48.349 --> 00:34:49.469
Sam's got your kids. Come on.

00:34:52.221 --> 00:34:53.315
Help!

00:34:53.972 --> 00:34:55.086
Please!

00:34:58.699 --> 00:34:59.813
Come here.

00:35:00.514 --> 00:35:02.106
Don't look, don't look.

00:35:15.454 --> 00:35:18.742
Sari, take your brother outside as
fast as you can and don't look back.

00:35:27.028 --> 00:35:28.617
Are you okay, baby?

00:35:28.640 --> 00:35:31.500
Sari, where's Sam? He's
inside. Something's got him.

00:35:53.772 --> 00:35:55.694
Ugh! Aah!

00:36:18.741 --> 00:36:19.319
Sam!

00:36:40.050 --> 00:36:40.881
Sam?!

00:36:41.782 --> 00:36:42.307
Sam!

00:36:47.062 --> 00:36:49.200
No, don't! Don't! What? Why?

00:36:50.513 --> 00:36:51.993
Because I know who it is.

00:36:52.769 --> 00:36:54.487
I can see her now.

00:37:11.613 --> 00:37:12.949
Mom.

00:37:23.264 --> 00:37:24.569
Dean.

00:37:39.916 --> 00:37:41.366
Sam.

00:37:47.844 --> 00:37:49.501
I'm sorry.

00:37:54.221 --> 00:37:55.883
F-For what?

00:38:08.190 --> 00:38:11.055
You, get out of my house.

00:38:11.872 --> 00:38:14.191
And let go of my son.

00:38:44.398 --> 00:38:45.970
Now it's over.

00:38:59.689 --> 00:39:00.943
Thanks for these.

00:39:01.455 --> 00:39:03.558
Don't thank me. They're yours.

00:39:08.269 --> 00:39:09.143
Well,

00:39:09.622 --> 00:39:13.218
There are no spirits in there
anymore, this time for sure.

00:39:14.402 --> 00:39:16.075
Not even my mom?

00:39:16.740 --> 00:39:18.075
No.

00:39:22.432 --> 00:39:23.921
What happened?

00:39:24.968 --> 00:39:29.625
Your mom's spirit and the poltergeists'
energy, they canceled each other out.

00:39:30.115 --> 00:39:33.704
Your mom destroyed herself
going after the thing.

00:39:34.961 --> 00:39:37.222
Why would she do something like that?

00:39:38.270 --> 00:39:41.349
Well, to protect her boys, of course.

00:39:49.224 --> 00:39:51.220
Sam, I'm sorry.

00:39:53.573 --> 00:39:54.963
For what?

00:39:55.493 --> 00:39:58.355
You sensed it was here, didn't you?

00:39:58.390 --> 00:40:00.115
Even when I couldn't.

00:40:05.123 --> 00:40:06.874
What's happening to me?

00:40:07.837 --> 00:40:10.839
I know I should have
all the answers, but...

00:40:12.540 --> 00:40:13.967
I don't know.

00:40:14.541 --> 00:40:15.984
Sam, you ready ?

00:40:21.044 --> 00:40:22.174
Bye.

00:40:25.167 --> 00:40:26.542
Bye Sam.

00:40:29.053 --> 00:40:30.213
Ah.

00:40:30.894 --> 00:40:33.235
Don't you boys be strangers.

00:40:33.658 --> 00:40:34.891
We won't.

00:40:36.438 --> 00:40:37.692
See you around.

00:41:08.999 --> 00:41:10.596
That boy...

00:41:12.228 --> 00:41:14.108
He has such

00:41:14.200 --> 00:41:16.195
Powerful abilities.

00:41:19.970 --> 00:41:22.707
Why he couldn't sense his own father,

00:41:22.919 --> 00:41:24.537
I have no idea.

00:41:30.289 --> 00:41:31.426
Mary's spirit...

00:41:33.219 --> 00:41:35.521
Do you really think she saved the boys?

00:41:37.860 --> 00:41:38.809
I do.

00:41:50.792 --> 00:41:53.515
John Winchester, I could just slap you.

00:41:53.581 --> 00:41:56.035
Why don't you go talk to your children?

00:41:57.667 --> 00:41:59.179
God, I want to.

00:42:01.164 --> 00:42:03.662
You have no idea how
much I want to see them.

00:42:06.602 --> 00:42:07.556
But I can't.

00:42:09.218 --> 00:42:09.923
Not yet.

00:42:16.463 --> 00:42:18.238
Not until I know the truth.



00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.000
